   7: 
   8: ## 1. Summary
   9: 
  10: The Virtual Office messaging drawer (`MessagingDrawer` → `MessageFeed` → `MessageComposer` / `MessageItem`, 
state in `MessagingContext`) already supports text, direct/group/room conversations, replies/threads, reactions, 
typing, manual history loading, and a basic read icon. Backend pieces exist for read receipts, attachment upload/read, 
and per-message stars, but the production drawer does not expose them as complete user workflows. This phase completes 
four timeline capabilities — read-receipt details, attachments, voice notes, starred filter — plus desktop 
notifications for new DM/group messages and loss-free failed sends, reusing existing APIs, repositories, hooks, and 
the TanStack Query cache.
  11: 
  12: ## 2. Problem statement
  13: 
  14: Workspace members chatting in the drawer cannot tell who actually read their message, cannot attach files from 
the production composer (its file button has no handler; the working upload composer only lives on a debug page), 
cannot send voice notes at all, cannot use stars (the menu entry exists but is not wired), and are not notified of new 
messages when the tab is in the background. These gaps make the messaging drawer insufficient for day-to-day office 
communication.
  15: 
  16: ## 3. Goals and success metrics
  17: 
  18: ### Goals
  19: - G1: A sender sees which members read their message and when.
  20: - G2: A user can attach files (pick, drag/drop, paste as Should) with progress and usable previews.
  21: - G3: A user can record, review, send, and play voice notes.
  22: - G4: A user can star messages and filter a conversation to their starred messages, reaching messages beyond the 
loaded page.
  23: - G5: A user is notified on the desktop of new DM/group messages when not looking at that conversation.
  24: - G6: No existing messaging behavior regresses; every database change reaches the online target in a controlled, 
verified way.
  25: 
  26: ### Success metrics
  27: - Two real accounts, in the production drawer, complete each flow without defects: read details (who + when), 
send/view files, send/play voice note, find an old starred message, receive a desktop notification. Each flow is 
covered by a passing two-account Playwright E2E test.
  28: - The existing-messaging regression E2E (text, reply/thread, reaction, typing, history, real-time delivery) 
passes after each slice.
  29: - Every migration written in this phase is recorded as applied to the online target `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko`, with 
catalog readback and smoke evidence, before the next task started.
  30: - Owner UAT in the browser accepts the phase.
  31: 
  32: ## 4. Users and stakeholders
  33: 
  34: ### Primary users
  35: - Workspace members who are members (`conversation_members`) of direct, group, or room conversations, acting as 
**sender** (author of a message) or **recipient** (any other member).
  36: 
  37: ### Secondary users
  38: - Users with a room microphone open in spatial audio (Phase 3) who record voice notes.
  39: 
  40: ### Stakeholders
  41: - Product owner (performs UAT, authorizes each online migration, owns application deployment).
  42: 
  43: ## 5. Scope
  44: 
  45: ### In scope
  46: - Production messaging drawer only, for `direct`, `group`, and `room` conversations.
  47: - Read-receipt details, read-marking rule, live receipt updates, unread counter alignment.
  48: - Attachments in the production composer and feed.
  49: - Voice notes (record, review, send, play), including room-microphone interaction.
  50: - Star/unstar and the per-conversation starred filter with jump-to-message.
  51: - Desktop notifications for new messages in DM and group conversations.
  52: - Preserving composer content when a send/upload fails (retry in place).
  53: - Replacing, in messaging test files this phase touches, tests that only mirror implementation with equivalent 
integration/E2E coverage (see BR-016).
  54: 
  55: ### Out of scope
  56: - Offline queue / automatic resend without network (Phase 5).
  57: - Missed-message recovery after reconnect and polling fallback (Phase 5); typing and multi-device sync changes 
(Phase 5). Existing behavior must not regress.
  58: - @mentions, notification rules (mute, room notifications), messaging metrics (Phase 5).
  59: - Message text search, automatic infinite scroll, "New messages" affordance (backlog).
  60: - Deleting or editing messages, removing attachments after send.
  61: - Voice transcription; inline PDF rendering; GIF autoplay requirements.
  62: - The debug page `src/app/debug/messaging-comparison`.
  63: - Broad cleanup of the test suite beyond touched messaging tests.
  64: - Application deployment (owner-owned).
  65: 
  66: ## 6. User journeys
  67: 
  68: - J1 Read details: Ana sends "Reunião às 15h" in a room. Bruno opens the drawer on that room with the tab 
focused and the message on screen → a receipt is recorded. Ana, with the conversation open, sees the indicator change 
live to "Lida por 1"; opening it shows Bruno, his avatar, and read time.
  69: - J2 Attachments: Ana drags 3 files (PNG, PDF, XLSX) into the composer, types optional text, watches per-file 
progress, removes one, and sends after the remaining uploads finish. Bruno sees an image thumbnail (opens a lightbox) 
and file cards with name, size, and download.
  70: - J3 Voice note: Ana, with the room mic open, clicks the mic button; the room mic auto-mutes with a visible 
notice; she records with live waveform and timer, stops, listens, and sends; the room mic returns to open. Bruno plays 
the note in the feed.
  71: - J4 Starred: Bruno stars a message, later toggles "Favoritas" in the conversation header, sees his starred 
messages newest-message-first, clicks an old one; the feed returns to normal, loads history with a loading indicator 
until it reaches the message, scrolls to it, and highlights it.
  72: - J5 Notification: Bruno has granted notification permission and has the tab in the background; Ana sends him a 
DM → Bruno receives a desktop notification.
  73: - J6 Failed send: Ana's send fails → her text and files remain in the composer with an error and "Tentar de 
novo".
  74: 
  75: ## 7. Functional requirements
  76: 
  77: | ID | Requirement | Priority | Acceptance signal |
  78: |---|---|---|---|
  79: | FR-001 | On messages the current user sent, show a read summary "Lida por N" (N = distinct non-sender readers) 
in direct, group, and room conversations. | Must | AC-001 |
  80: | FR-002 | Opening the read summary (click, and keyboard) shows each reader's avatar, name, and read time, most 
recent first. No denominator and no "not read" list. | Must | AC-002 |
  81: | FR-003 | Reader identities and times are exposed by the application UI and application API only to the 
message's sender. | Must | AC-003 |
  82: | FR-004 | A receipt is recorded for a recipient only when the message is rendered visibly on screen, with the 
drawer open on that conversation and the browser tab visible/focused. Sender messages never produce receipts. | Must | 
AC-004, AC-005 |
  83: | FR-005 | While the sender has the conversation open, the read summary and reader list update in real time when 
a recipient reads. | Must | AC-006 |
  84: | FR-006 | The conversation-list unread counter decreases only as messages are marked read under FR-004. | Must 
| AC-007 |
  85: | FR-007 | The production composer accepts files via the file picker and via drag-and-drop onto the 
composer/drawer. | Must | AC-008 |
  86: | FR-008 | A message may carry up to 5 files, each ≤ 10 MB, of types JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, PDF, TXT, DOC, DOCX, 
XLS, XLSX; text is optional; attachment-only messages are allowed. Violations are rejected with a clear message before 
upload and enforced server-side. | Must | AC-009, AC-010 |
  87: | FR-009 | Each pending file shows upload progress and can be removed/cancelled; the message is sent only after 
all its uploads complete; an upload failure shows an error and a retry action. | Must | AC-011, AC-012 |
  88: | FR-010 | Files from cancelled, removed, or failed uploads are never visible to any user and are deleted from 
storage; files not attached to a sent message are never visible to anyone. | Must | AC-013 |
