 105: ## 8. Business rules
 106: 
 107: | ID | Rule | Rationale |
 108: |---|---|---|
 109: | BR-001 | "Read" = the message was visibly rendered on the recipient's screen with the drawer open on that 
conversation and the tab visible/focused. Opening a conversation does not by itself mark unseen messages read. | 
Faithful to actual reading (R1-q4). |
 110: | BR-002 | A sender never generates a read receipt for their own message. | R1-q16-B. |
 111: | BR-003 | Only the message's sender can see reader identities/times. Receipts are always on; there is no 
opt-out. | R1-q5. |
 112: | BR-004 | The summary shows only "Lida por N" and the readers list; no "of M" denominator and no unread-members 
list. | Membership changes over time (R2-q11). |
 113: | BR-005 | The unread counter follows BR-001 (example: 20 unread, only the last 5 seen → counter shows 15 until 
the user scrolls). | R3-b. |
 114: | BR-006 | Attachments: max 5 per message, 10 MB each, allowlist per FR-008; audio types only for voice notes. | 
Existing server/bucket limits (R1-q6, q7). |
 115: | BR-007 | A message with attachments is created only after all its uploads succeed; no partially-attached 
message is ever visible. | R1-q9. |
 116: | BR-008 | Voice notes are at most 2 minutes. | R1-q11. |
 117: | BR-009 | Stars are personal; the starred list is ordered by message date, newest first. | R2-q14. |
 118: | BR-010 | Desktop notifications only for others' messages in direct/group conversations, only when the tab is 
hidden or the drawer is not open on that conversation. | R2-q3. |
 119: | BR-011 | Attachments and voice notes are reachable only by conversation members via short-lived signed URLs; 
never by public URL. | R1-q16-A. |
 120: | BR-012 | Migration gate (amended 2026-10-04 by the owner): during the phase every migration is applied to the 
local database and tested only. When all other phase work is complete, all phase migrations are applied to the online 
target `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` together, after the owner is notified (migration list, target, rollback) and gives OK, 
followed by catalog readback and a smoke check. The phase is not complete until this is done. | R1-q17 note, R2-q6 
note, R3-a; amendment: owner 2026-10-04 ("vamos fazer isso quando toda a fase estiver finalizada"). |
 121: | BR-013 | Every migration is additive/backward compatible with the currently published application. | R2-q7. |
 122: | BR-014 | No new paid service (storage tier, transcoding, media SaaS). | R1-q16-D. |
 123: | BR-015 | Identity: RLS and routes resolve the app user via `users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text`; foreign 
keys use `users.id`; never compare `users.id` with `auth.uid()`. | R1-q16-E. |
 124: | BR-016 | Tests: new tests are integration and E2E; unit tests only when strictly necessary, with written 
justification. In messaging test files this phase touches, tests that only mirror implementation are replaced by 
equivalent integration/E2E coverage and then removed, each removal recorded with reason in TRACK; no test is removed 
without equivalent coverage. | R1-q18 note, R2-q8. |
 125: | BR-017 | Existing drawer behavior must not regress: text, replies/threads, reactions, typing, history loading, 
real-time delivery, current reconnect. | R1-q16-C, R2-q2. |
 126: 
 127: ## 9. Data and integrations
 128: 
 129: ### Data inputs
 130: - `message_read_receipts(id, message_id, user_id, read_at, conversation_id)` — existing; member-visible SELECT 
policy `read_receipts_in_own_conversations`; in the Realtime publication.
 131: - `conversation_members` — membership for direct/group/room (`private.is_conversation_member`).
 132: - Message attachments metadata and the private `attachments` storage bucket (existing upload/read routes: 
`src/app/api/messages/upload/route.ts`, `src/app/api/messages/attachment/[id]/route.ts`).
 133: - Message stars (existing route `src/app/api/messages/[messageId]/star/route.ts`, repository 
`getStarredMessages(userId, conversationId?)`; no list route exists yet).
 134: - Voice-note metadata: duration and waveform (type `VoiceNoteAttachment` exists).
 135: 
 136: ### Data outputs
 137: - Receipts written per BR-001; reader details returned to the sender only.
 138: - Attachment and voice-note records linked to sent messages; storage objects deleted for cancelled/failed 
uploads.
 139: - Paginated starred-message results per user and conversation.
 140: 
 141: ### Integrations
 142: - Supabase Postgres, Storage, Auth, Realtime (existing project contracts).
 143: - Browser APIs: MediaRecorder/getUserMedia (voice), Notifications API, Page Visibility, 
IntersectionObserver-equivalent visibility detection, Drag and Drop, Clipboard.
 144: - Phase 3 spatial-audio microphone state (mute/restore during recording).
 145: 
 146: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
 147: 
 148: ### Constraints
 149: - Next.js App Router, React, strict TypeScript, Supabase, TanStack Query, shadcn/ui/Radix; reuse existing 
repositories/routes/hooks; server routes use `createSupabaseServerClient` and `auth.getUser()`.
 150: - Browser floor: Chrome and Edge desktop mandatory; Firefox/Safari best effort.
 151: - Limits: 10 MB per file, 5 files per message, voice ≤ 2 min.
 152: - Database: local only during the phase; all phase migrations applied online together at phase end after the 
owner's OK (BR-012, amended 2026-10-04); additive migrations (BR-013); online target `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` 
(historical migration-provenance concern must be preflighted before the first online application).
 153: - Application deployment is owned by the owner; this phase ends with the application verified locally against 
the online database.
 154: - No new paid services.
 155: 
 156: ### Assumptions
 157: Only assumptions explicitly confirmed by the user:
 158: - Delivery in ordered slices within this single SPEC (e.g., receipts + starred → attachments → voice), with 
notifications and failed-send preservation placed by the plan (R1-q1).
 159: 
 160: ## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
 161: 
 162: | Case | Expected behavior |
 163: |---|---|
 164: | Recipient has the drawer open but the tab in background | No receipt; receipt recorded when the tab becomes 
visible with the message on screen. |
 165: | Recipient opens a conversation with 20 unread, sees only last 5 | 5 receipts; unread counter shows 15 until 
scrolling reveals the rest. |
 166: | Sender views own message | No receipt for the sender; summary counts only other members. |
 167: | Non-sender member tries to get reader details (UI or app API) | Not shown/denied. |
 168: | Room with many readers | Reader list scrolls; most recent first. |
 169: | File > 10 MB, disallowed type, or a 6th file | Rejected before upload with a clear message; server also 
rejects. |
 170: | One of several uploads fails | Error on that file with retry; message not sent until all succeed or the file 
is removed. |
 171: | User cancels/removes a pending file | Upload aborted; stored object deleted; never visible. |
 172: | User closes the tab mid-upload | No message is created; the file is never visible to anyone. |
 173: | Send fails (network/server error) | Text, reply target, and files stay in the composer with error and retry. |
 174: | Non-member requests an attachment URL/ID | Denied; no public URL exists. |
 175: | Mic permission denied / no device / unsupported | Clear message; text and attachments work; record disabled 
when unsupported. |
 176: | Recording reaches 2 minutes | Auto-stops; warning shown from 1:50. |
 177: | Room mic open when recording starts | Muted with notice; restored on stop/discard/send. Room mic previously 
muted → remains muted. |
 178: | Chrome-recorded note opened in Safari/Firefox | Plays, or shows a clear "cannot play" message. |
 179: | Starred message is older than loaded history | History loads with indicator until reached; scroll + highlight. 
|
 180: | Starred message no longer accessible (user left/removed from conversation) | Notice; feed stays stable. |
 181: | User stars on one device | Star state appears on the user's other devices after refresh/cache update. |
 182: | Notification permission denied/unsupported | No notifications; messaging unaffected. |
 183: | New DM while the user is viewing that DM with the tab visible | No notification. |
 184: | New room message while tab hidden | No notification (rooms excluded). |
 185: | Realtime reconnects | Existing reconnect continues working; receipts/stars/attachments consistent after 
reconnect. |
 186: 
 187: ## 12. Security, privacy, compliance, and abuse considerations
 188: 
 189: - Attachments/voice in a private bucket; reads via short-lived signed URLs after membership authorization 
(BR-011).
 190: - Reader details restricted to the sender at the application UI/API (BR-003). The current RLS lets any member 
select all receipts of a conversation; whether table-level reads are also narrowed is decided in planning subject to 
BR-013 compatibility, and recorded.
 191: - Server-side enforcement of size/type/count limits; audio MIME accepted only for voice notes; per-message 
attachment cap limits abuse.
 192: - Authorization via `auth.getUser()`; service role never replaces membership checks; identity per BR-015.
 193: - Every migration, RLS/storage policy, repository, or route change passes the Supabase/RLS review gate.
 194: 
 195: ## 13. Accessibility, localization, and usability considerations
 196: 
 197: - All new controls (attach, remove/cancel, retry, record/stop/send/discard, play/pause, star, starred filter, 
reader list) are keyboard operable with screen-reader labels.
 198: - Works at the current drawer width, including narrow screens.
 199: - UI copy follows the existing application language (Portuguese strings such as "Lida por N").
 200: - Portal menus/popovers stop pointer/click/key propagation per project UI rules.
 201: 
 202: ## 14. Acceptance criteria
 203: 
 204: - AC-001 (FR-001, BR-004): Given A sent a message in a direct, a group, and a room conversation, when 1 or more 
other members read it, then A sees "Lida por N" with N equal to the distinct non-sender readers, with no denominator.
 205: - AC-002 (FR-002, BR-004): Given a message read by B then C, when A opens the summary by click or keyboard, then 
A sees C then B with avatar, name, and read time, and no not-read list.
 206: - AC-003 (FR-003, BR-003): Given B (non-sender member) and A's message read by C, when B views the message and 
calls the application API for its details, then B sees no reader identities/times and the API returns no reader 
details to B.
 207: - AC-004 (FR-004, BR-001, BR-005): Given B has the drawer open on the conversation, when the message is 
off-screen or the tab is hidden, then no receipt exists; when the tab is visible and the message is on screen, then a 
receipt exists. Given 20 unread and only 5 visible, then exactly 5 receipts exist.
 208: - AC-005 (FR-004, BR-002): Given A views their own messages, then no receipt with A's user is created for them.
 209: - AC-006 (FR-005): Given A has the conversation open, when B reads A's message, then A's summary/list updates 
without reload.
 210: - AC-007 (FR-006, BR-005): Given B has 20 unread in a conversation, when B opens it and sees only the last 5, 
then the list counter shows 15; after scrolling all into view, it shows 0.
 211: - AC-008 (FR-007): Given the production drawer, when A picks files via the file button or drops files onto the 
composer, then they appear as pending attachments.
 212: - AC-009 (FR-008, BR-006): Given A adds a 6th file, a file > 10 MB, or a disallowed type, then it is rejected 
with a clear message before upload; a direct request bypassing the UI is rejected by the server.
 213: - AC-010 (FR-008): Given A sends a message with attachments and no text, then B receives an attachment-only 
message.
 214: - AC-011 (FR-009, BR-007): Given A sends 3 files, then per-file progress is shown and B sees the message only 
after all 3 uploads complete, never partially attached.
 215: - AC-012 (FR-009): Given one upload fails, then that file shows an error and retry; retry succeeds and the 
message can be sent.
 216: - AC-013 (FR-010): Given A removes/cancels a pending file or an upload fails and is abandoned, then the storage 
object is deleted (or never referenced) and no user can see it; given A closes the tab mid-upload, then no message 
exists and the file is not visible.
 217: - AC-014 (FR-011): Given B receives an image and a PDF, then B sees an inline thumbnail that opens a larger view 
and a card with icon, name, size, and download.
 218: - AC-015 (FR-011, BR-011): Given C is not a member, when C requests the attachment via the application API or a 
guessed storage path, then access is denied; given a member, content loads via a signed URL that expires.
 219: - AC-016 (FR-012, Should): Given an image in the clipboard, when A presses Ctrl+V in the composer, then it 
becomes a pending attachment.
 220: - AC-017 (FR-013, FR-015, FR-019): Given Chrome or Edge with mic permission, when A records, stops, previews, 
and sends a voice note, then a live waveform and timer were shown during recording, and both A and B can play it with 
play/pause, duration, and progress.
 221: - AC-018 (FR-014, BR-008): Given A records continuously, then a warning appears at 1:50 and recording auto-stops 
at 2:00 with the note ready to preview/send.
 222: - AC-019 (FR-016): Given A's room mic is open, when A starts recording, then the room mic is muted with a 
visible notice; after send, discard, or stop, it returns to open; given it was muted, it remains muted.
 223: - AC-020 (FR-017): Given mic permission is denied (or no device/unsupported), when A tries to record, then a 
clear reason and guidance appear, and A can still send text and files; when unsupported, the record button is disabled 
with explanation.
 224: - AC-021 (FR-018, BR-006, BR-011): Given a voice note is sent, then it is stored in the private attachments 
storage with duration and waveform metadata; given an audio file is uploaded as a regular attachment, then it is 
rejected.
 225: - AC-022 (FR-019): Given a note recorded in Chrome, when opened in Firefox or Safari, then it plays or shows a 
clear cannot-play message (checked at least once per browser available; result recorded).
 226: - AC-023 (FR-020, BR-009): Given A stars a message, then the star shows for A on that message and on A's other 
session after refresh, B sees no star from A, and unstarring removes it.
 227: - AC-024 (FR-021, BR-009): Given A starred messages including one older than the first loaded page, when A 
toggles the starred filter, then A sees only their starred messages in that conversation ordered by message date 
newest first, including the old one, with pagination; toggling back restores the normal feed.
 228: - AC-025 (FR-022): Given A selects an old starred result, then the normal feed loads history with a visible 
loading indicator until the message is present, scrolls to it, and highlights it.
 229: - AC-026 (FR-022): Given the starred message is no longer accessible to A, when A selects it, then a notice 
appears and the feed remains stable (no error screen, no infinite loading).
 230: - AC-027 (FR-023, BR-010): Given B granted permission via an explicit action, when A sends B a DM or a group 
message while B's tab is hidden or the drawer is not on that conversation, then B gets a desktop notification; when B 
is viewing that conversation with the tab visible, or the message is B's own, or it is a room message, then no 
notification.
 231: - AC-028 (FR-023): Given notification permission is denied or unsupported, then no notification is attempted and 
messaging works normally.
 232: - AC-029 (FR-024): Given a send fails, then the text, reply target, and pending files remain in the composer 
with an error and retry; retry sends exactly one message.
 233: - AC-030 (FR-025, BR-017): Given the Realtime connection drops and the existing reconnect restores it, then 
receipts, stars, and attachment messages displayed match the server, and existing reconnect behavior is unchanged.
 234: - AC-031 (BR-017): After each slice, the regression E2E covering text send, reply/thread, reaction, typing 
indicator, history loading, and real-time delivery between two accounts passes.
 235: - AC-032 (BR-012, amended 2026-10-04): For every migration created in this phase, TRACK records local 
application + passing tests; at phase end, TRACK records the owner notification (list, target, rollback), the owner's 
OK, online application of every phase migration to `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko`, catalog readback, and smoke result.
 236: - AC-033 (BR-013): Each migration is reviewed as additive, and after online application the existing (pre-phase) 
messaging flows smoke-checked against the online database still work.
 237: - AC-034 (BR-014): The phase diff adds no paid service, SDK, or storage/transcoding provider; dependency 
additions (if any) are free and listed in TRACK.
 238: - AC-035 (BR-015, BR-011): The Supabase/RLS review gate passes for every migration, policy, repository, and 
route change, including the users.id vs supabase_uid check.
 239: - AC-036 (BR-016): New tests are integration/E2E; any unit test added carries a written justification; every 
removed test is listed in TRACK with reason and the replacing integration/E2E test.
 240: - AC-037 (Section 13): New controls are reachable and operable by keyboard with accessible names, and the drawer 
flows work at narrow width (verified in E2E or recorded manual check).
 241: 
 242: ## 15. Test strategy
 243: 
 244: - Test levels:
 245:   - Integration (local Supabase Postgres/Storage): receipt write rules (visibility-driven API, no sender 
receipts), sender-only reader-detail API, attachment limits/MIME/count, signed-URL authorization and non-member 
denial, orphan cleanup, starred list pagination/order, any new RPC/route/policy and its RLS.
 246:   - E2E (Playwright, two real authenticated accounts, Chrome): one test per flow — receipts (incl. live update 
and unread counter), attachments (pick/drag, progress, failure/retry, previews), voice (fake media device; 
record/preview/send/play; 2-min limit can use a test-configurable clock if needed without changing the product limit; 
room-mic mute/restore), starred (filter, old message jump, inaccessible notice), notifications (granted/denied 
permission, hidden tab), failed-send preservation, reconnect consistency, and the existing-messaging regression suite.
 247:   - Unit: only when strictly necessary (e.g., a pure waveform/duration computation that cannot be meaningfully 
covered otherwise), with justification recorded.
 248: - TDD from acceptance criteria where practical: each test names its AC ID.
 249: - Test data: two seeded accounts in the same company with a direct, a group, and a room conversation; a 
conversation with > 1 page of history containing an old starred message; sample files of each allowed type, an 
oversized file, and a disallowed type.
 250: - Environments: local Supabase for integration/E2E; online target only for post-migration readback and smoke 
(BR-012); Firefox/Safari checks recorded best effort.
 251: - Existing tests: handled per BR-016.
 252: - Mandatory failure-path tests: oversized/disallowed/6th file, upload failure + retry, cancel/remove cleanup, 
non-member attachment access, non-sender reader-detail access, mic denied/unsupported, notification denied, send 
failure preservation, inaccessible starred message.
 253: - Completion also requires `npm run type-check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` passing.
 254: 
 255: ## 16. Validation and launch checklist
 256: 
 257: - All Must FRs and AC-001..AC-037 (except AC-016 as Should) have evidence in TRACK.
 258: - Every migration applied online per BR-012 with readback and smoke recorded (AC-032/AC-033).
 259: - Supabase/RLS review gate passed (AC-035).
 260: - Type-check, lint, build, integration, and E2E pass; regression suite passes.
 261: - Owner UAT in the browser with two accounts.
 262: - Hand-off states the application is ready to deploy against the online database; deployment is performed by the 
owner.
 263: 
 264: ## 17. Open questions
 265: 
 266: Non-blocking; resolved in planning/execution with evidence:
 267: - Whether to also narrow table-level RLS on `message_read_receipts` to the sender/own rows, if compatible with 
the published app (BR-013).
 268: - Exact audio container/codec meeting the Chrome/Edge floor and the Safari/Firefox best-effort rule.
 269: - Desktop-notification click behavior beyond the browser default (focusing the window); opening the specific 
conversation may be added if trivial and is not a gate.
 270: - Storage reclamation for uploads abandoned by closing the tab (they are never visible per FR-010); a scheduled 
job is not required by this SPEC.

