 139: ## 9. Data and integrations
 140: 
 141: ### Data inputs
 142: - Composer text, reply target, and mention selections (user IDs) per message.
 143: - Browser connectivity events (`online`/`offline`), Realtime channel status, tab visibility.
 144: - Server responses from `POST /api/messages/create` (status, `clientMessageId` replay, rate-limit retry delay 
when present).
 145: 
 146: ### Data outputs
 147: - Browser IndexedDB outbox, keyed by application user ID: `clientMessageId`, conversation ID, text, reply 
target, mention user IDs, created-at, attempt state, failure reason. Deleted per BR-007/BR-008; never shared across 
users.
 148: - Database: message mention records (message ID + mentioned application user ID), readable under the same 
conversation-membership rules as the message.
 149: - Realtime authorization policy for private typing topics (members only).
 150: - `mark_conversation_read` with an internal membership check; `get_unread_counts` without `anon` EXECUTE.
 151: - Structured metric log lines (BR-013) from an authenticated application route.
 152: - Persisted drawer state per user: open flag + active conversation ID (browser storage).
 153: 
 154: ### Integrations
 155: - Supabase Postgres, Realtime (`postgres_changes`, private broadcast topics with RLS on `realtime.messages`), 
Auth (server routes use `createSupabaseServerClient` + `auth.getUser()`).
 156: - Browser APIs: IndexedDB, Web Locks/BroadcastChannel or equivalent for cross-tab coordination, Notification API 
(existing Phase 4), Page Visibility.
 157: - Hosting logs (Vercel) and/or Supabase logs as the metrics sink — no new external analytics dependency.
 158: 
 159: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
 160: 
 161: ### Constraints
 162: - Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, API 
routes, and query keys (`['messages', id]`, `['conversations', userId]`, …) rather than parallel implementations.
 163: - Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages 
link to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
 164: - Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated), Firefox desktop. Safari and mobile not required.
 165: - Background notifications are page-level only (tab open but hidden); no service worker.
 166: - No message text or names in metrics (BR-013); no new external analytics service.
 167: - The sign-out confirmation must not change the existing presence logout sequence (presence-safety rules apply 
to that touch point).
 168: - Online database changes only at phase end with explicit authorization (BR-014); the hosted app currently runs 
the pre-Phase-4 build until the owner deploys.
 169: - Repository test policy (BR-015); type-check, lint, and build must pass.
 170: 
 171: ### Assumptions
 172: - None beyond the user-confirmed answers recorded in `state.md`.
