 174: ## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
 175: 
 176: | Case | Expected behavior |
 177: |---|---|
 178: | Request reaches the server but the response is lost | Message stays pending; the retry reuses 
`clientMessageId`; server returns the stored message; exactly one message exists (AC-038). |
 179: | Two tabs come online at the same time with the same outbox | Only one tab sends each message; each is stored 
and shown once (AC-005). |
 180: | User cancels in tab 2 while tab 1 is about to send | Cancel only while waiting; once in flight the item shows 
"enviando" without cancel; no message sent after a completed cancel (AC-006). |
 181: | Lost access to the conversation before reconnect | First message fails definitively with text kept; later 
messages of that conversation wait; other conversations deliver (AC-007). |
 182: | Access regained after a definitive failure | "Tentar de novo" delivers it; then the waiting messages deliver 
in order (AC-008). |
 183: | Server rate limit during drain | Messages stay pending and retry automatically; order and uniqueness preserved 
(AC-009). |
 184: | Laptop asleep > 24 h with pending messages | They become "expirada" failures, not sent automatically (AC-010). 
|
 185: | Offline message with attachment or voice note | Not queued; Phase 4 composer failure + retry (AC-011). |
 186: | Session expires while messages are pending; another user signs in on the same browser | The other user never 
sees or sends them; the original user's messages drain after they sign in again (AC-012). |
 187: | User clicks Sair with pending messages | Confirmation dialog; Cancelar keeps everything; Sair mesmo deletes 
the outbox and signs out (AC-013). |
 188: | IndexedDB unavailable (private mode, blocked storage) | Queue cannot persist: message keeps the Phase 4 
composer failure + "Tentar de novo" — never silently dropped (AC-039). |
 189: | Realtime drop shorter than 5 s | No "Reconectando…" banner (AC-014). |
 190: | Realtime down > 30 s, tab hidden | No polling; on becoming visible, fetch immediately then every 15 s 
(AC-016). |
 191: | Realtime back after polling | Polling requests stop; catch-up shows no duplicates (AC-015, AC-016). |
 192: | Typist closes the tab or loses connection mid-typing | Indicator disappears ≤ 5 s (AC-017). |
 193: | Non-member tries to join a typing topic | Join refused / no events received (AC-019). |
 194: | "@name" for a non-member or forged mention ID in a direct API call | No mention recorded, no notification 
(AC-024). |
 195: | Mention in a DM that would also notify as a DM | Exactly one notification (AC-026). |
 196: | Mentioned user is viewing that conversation in a visible tab | No notification (AC-026). |
 197: | Metrics route down or slow | Messaging unaffected, no visible error (AC-029). |
 198: | Restored conversation no longer accessible after reload | Conversation list opens without error (AC-032). |
