 102:   unread/read sync, R7 @mention desktop notifications. R6 metrics NOT selected.
 103: - R1-q2 "reliable" = A no message silently lost (delivers or visible failure
 104:   with action); B never duplicates (auto-resend, several tabs); C pending
 105:   messages deliver within ~10 s after connectivity returns without clicks;
 106:   D with Realtime down, others' new messages appear within ~30–45 s via
 107:   polling; E offline-sent order preserved.
 108: - R1-q3 A: queue in IndexedDB per user; survives reload/close; deleted on logout.
 109: - R1-q4 A: queue only text + replies; attachments/voice offline keep the
 110:   Phase 4 failure-in-composer + "Tentar de novo".
 111: - R1-q5 A in order, one at a time per conversation, later ones wait if one
 112:   fails; B pending shown in feed with clock state, cancellable before sending;
 113:   C definitive rejection (lost access, invalid content, rate limit) stops
 114:   retrying, shows failure with text preserved; D pending expires after a time
 115:   (example 24 h) and becomes a visible failure without auto-send. E (edit
 116:   pending) not selected.
 117: - R1-q6 A: discreet banner at the top of the chat ("Sem conexão — mensagens
 118:   serão enviadas quando voltar" / "Reconectando…"), hides itself when normal.
 119: - R1-q7 A: poll every 15 s, only while tab visible: open conversation +
 120:   conversation list (unread); stops as soon as Realtime returns.
 121: - R1-q8 A keeps showing during continuous typing, disappears ~5 s after stop;
 122:   B names ("Ana está digitando…", "Ana e Bruno…", "3 pessoas…"); C DM, group,
 123:   room; D private channel, only conversation members receive typing; E never
 124:   show my own typing from my other tabs/devices.
 125: - R1-q9 A unread counter + read state sync live across my devices; B messages
 126:   I sent from another device appear immediately. C stars, D drafts, E
 127:   cross-device notification dismissal NOT selected.
 128: - R1-q10 A typing @ opens member list of the conversation, choosing inserts a
 129:   highlighted mention; B mentioned user gets desktop notification even in a
 130:   ROOM; E mention valid only for conversation members, otherwise plain text.
 131:   C (notify even with DM/group notifications off) and D (@todos/@here) NOT
 132:   selected.
 133: - R1-q11 A: background = tab open but hidden/minimized (Phase 4 model); no
 134:   service worker / Web Push.
 135: - R1-q12 B: metrics, if included, as technical logs only (Supabase/Vercel), no
 136:   UI. (Conflicts with R1-q1 not selecting R6 → asked in round 2.)
 137: - R1-q13 A: migrations local during the phase; online at phase end with
 138:   explicit authorization; app deployment stays with the user.
 139: - R1-q14 A Chrome + Edge desktop (automated), B Firefox desktop. Safari and
 140:   mobile NOT selected.
 141: - R1-q15 Phase 4 follow-ups in scope: A DB — membership check in
 142:   mark_conversation_read and block anon from get_unread_counts; C restore the
 143:   open conversation after page reload. B, D, E, F not selected.
 144: - R1-q16 Must never happen: A one user's pending message sent by another user
 145:   who later logs in on the same browser; B duplicates when two tabs drain the
 146:   same queue; C notification for my own message or the conversation I'm
 147:   viewing; D polling continuing after Realtime returned; E typing stuck after
 148:   the person left/closed the tab; F mention notifying a non-member.
 149: - R1-q17 A: acceptance like Phase 4 — two-account E2E (simulated internet and
 150:   Realtime outages) + local DB integration tests + owner final test against the
 151:   online DB. (Repo policy: no unit tests.)
 152: - R1-q18 A: all company members who use chat (DM, group, room); no admin
 153:   specifics except possibly metrics.
