   5: -- The drawer composer generates one key (uuid) per composition and resends it
   6: -- on every "Tentar de novo" of that composition. POST /api/messages/create
   7: -- stores it in messages.client_message_id; a create repeating a key already
   8: -- stored for the same sender and conversation returns the existing message
   9: -- instead of inserting another. When a committed create loses its response
  10: -- and the user retries, the server therefore keeps exactly one row.
  11: --
  12: -- Scope of uniqueness: (sender_id, conversation_id, client_message_id). The
  13: -- sender is always the authenticated caller resolved on the server
  14: -- (users.supabase_uid = auth.uid() -> users.id), so one user's key can never
  15: -- match or block another user's message, and a key reused in another
  16: -- conversation is a different message.
  17: --
  18: -- Concurrency: two simultaneous creates with the same key race on this unique
  19: -- index; the loser gets unique_violation (23505), which the repository turns
  20: -- into a read of the winning row (no 500, one row).
