The review now has enough evidence for a revision verdict. The SPEC treats a timed-out send as cancellable even when 
the server may already have stored it, and join-time typing authorization does not enforce membership changes on an 
existing connection. The remaining findings concern mention atomicity, logout races, metrics validation, and AC 
coverage.
